    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d6dad40e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme features a photo of comedian Steve Harvey, who is smiling broadly while seated at a panel. The text overlay reads: \"when your put in fb jail ..but your not... even sweatin cause of your back up account.\" The intent is to humorously depict a person who is unaffected by Facebook's account suspension because they have a backup account. The meme uses Steve Harvey's recognizable, cheerful expression to contrast with the implied frustration or inconvenience of being temporarily banned from a social media platform. While the content is lighthearted and not directly abusive or hateful toward any specific group, it does contain a potentially harmful element: it trivializes the experience of being banned from a major social media platform, which can be a significant disruption for many users. The humor relies on the absurdity of having a backup account, which may not be accessible or practical for everyone, and could unintentionally normalize or downplay the real-world consequences of social media bans, such as loss of communication, professional impact, or emotional distress. The meme does not contain any explicit racist, sexist, anti-Semitic, or other targeted hate content, but its humor is derived from a situation that could be seen as dismissive of the real-world impact of digital platform restrictions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_35ee7307"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
